WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:04.835
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.837 --> 00:08.139
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:08.141 --> 00:11.876
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.878 --> 00:14.878
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.880 --> 00:18.281
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.283 --> 00:21.718
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.720 --> 00:23.386
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:23.388 --> 00:25.021
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:25.023 --> 00:29.758
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.232 --> 00:38.635
<i>Man: You shower
with your dog every day.</i>

00:38.637 --> 00:40.736
<i>Do you and your dog use
the same soap?</i>

00:40.738 --> 00:43.672
<i>If so, one of you
is damaging your hair.</i>

00:43.674 --> 00:45.741
Really?
(concerned grunt)

00:45.743 --> 00:48.510
<i>Dial cross species
is specially formulated</i>

00:48.512 --> 00:50.512
<i>For both humans and dogs.</i>

00:50.514 --> 00:52.146
<i>You'll like
that it gets you clean.</i>

00:52.148 --> 00:53.816
<i>He'll like
that it smells like beef.</i>

00:53.818 --> 00:55.650
That sounds great!
(knocking)

00:55.652 --> 00:58.420
Woman: Jim, are you showering
with the dog again?

00:58.422 --> 00:59.687
What the hell?!

00:59.689 --> 01:00.989
All right, peter,
I'm leaving.

01:00.991 --> 01:02.924
Bonnie invited me to
the shooting range.

01:02.926 --> 01:04.159
What?

01:04.161 --> 01:06.527
Yeah, bonnie says
she goes every week.

01:06.529 --> 01:09.130
(yelling)

01:11.400 --> 01:12.900
(panting)

01:12.902 --> 01:15.536
I think next time
you should bring someone else.

01:15.538 --> 01:18.071
Now, you'll be watching stewie,
and I don't want you just

01:18.073 --> 01:19.874
To prop him up next
to the tv all day.

01:19.876 --> 01:21.508
Take him to
the park.

01:21.510 --> 01:22.844
I want him to get
some fresh air.

01:22.846 --> 01:24.778
Fresh air is bad
for a kid, lois.

01:24.780 --> 01:26.379
Look at michael j. Fox.

01:26.381 --> 01:27.748
What?
I don't know.

01:27.750 --> 01:29.282
Peter, you are taking
stewie to the park.

01:29.284 --> 01:31.618
It'll do you good to spend
some time with your son.

01:31.620 --> 01:33.587
I spend lots of time
with him, lois.

01:33.589 --> 01:35.722
Just last week,
I took him to the doctor.

01:35.724 --> 01:38.458
Mr. Griffin, you're here
to get your prostate examined?

01:38.460 --> 01:40.760
Yeah, this is me.

01:44.765 --> 01:46.767
Is that your
little one there?

01:46.769 --> 01:49.603
Oh, no, it's-it's just
the way I'm sitting.

01:49.605 --> 01:51.604
Ah, nothing like a day
at the park,

01:51.606 --> 01:54.707
Surrounded by overcompensating
divorced dads.

01:54.709 --> 01:56.576
Wow! Look how high
you're going!

01:56.578 --> 01:58.410
What an amazing day this is!

01:58.412 --> 01:59.745
(laughs)

01:59.747 --> 02:02.114
Is mommy spending
$2,500 a month on you?

02:02.116 --> 02:04.316
Because that's what
I'm sending mommy!

02:04.318 --> 02:06.484
Oh, my god,
it's only been five minutes,

02:06.486 --> 02:09.522
And I'm already bored
out of my mind.

02:11.725 --> 02:14.125
Damn, I wish I could go
to the clam.

02:16.128 --> 02:20.064
Aah! Well, I guess
I see those guys all the time.

02:23.769 --> 02:25.803
A clown?!
Eh, well, I guess

02:25.805 --> 02:28.173
What's the big deal, huh?
It's just one.

02:34.580 --> 02:38.316
Oh, I was quite sure it was just
one from the size of the car!

02:38.318 --> 02:39.650
(phone ringing)
hello?

02:39.652 --> 02:40.984
Quagmire:
Peter, where the hell are you?

02:40.986 --> 02:42.252
You got to get down
to the clam, man.

02:42.254 --> 02:43.754
There's, like,
60 clowns in here.

02:43.756 --> 02:45.522
Ugh, I can't.
I got to watch stewie.

02:45.524 --> 02:48.925
Joe:
Peter, they threw what I thought
was a bucket of water on me,

02:48.927 --> 02:51.794
But it turns out,
it was just a bunch of confetti!

02:51.796 --> 02:53.797
Oh, man, I got
to get over there!

02:53.799 --> 02:55.832
(phone beeps off)

02:58.802 --> 03:02.438
Okay, okay. It's okay
as long as I can still see him.

03:02.440 --> 03:04.174
Okay, stewie, there you are.

03:04.176 --> 03:05.675
There you are, safe and sound.

03:05.677 --> 03:08.010
Daddy can still see you.

03:09.112 --> 03:11.346
Okay, daddy
can still see you.

03:11.348 --> 03:13.950
Daddy can still see you.

03:19.890 --> 03:22.791
Daddy can still see you.

03:33.236 --> 03:37.571
That was a wink, but you don't
know it 'cause it's just a eye.

03:40.842 --> 03:43.477
<i>Man (over tv):
We now return to superman.</i>

03:43.479 --> 03:45.312
(all crying)

03:45.314 --> 03:46.814
Lois, what's wrong?

03:46.816 --> 03:48.716
Clark, we all have
breast cancer!

03:48.718 --> 03:51.552
The doctor says it's as if
our breasts have been x-rayed

03:51.554 --> 03:54.855
Five hours a day, every day,
for the last three years!

03:54.857 --> 03:56.824
Oh, my god,
that's terrible.

03:56.826 --> 03:59.893
First, every woman I've ever
known, and now you guys.

03:59.895 --> 04:01.395
(sighs):
Ah!

04:01.397 --> 04:03.863
Boy, it was smart
to wait out that thunderstorm.

04:03.865 --> 04:06.266
(phone ringing)
aah, it's lois!

04:06.268 --> 04:07.834
Oh, my god! Stewie!

04:07.836 --> 04:09.602
Oh, uh, hey, lois.

04:09.604 --> 04:11.004
H-hey, it's hard to hear you

04:11.006 --> 04:13.172
Over the sound
of joyful children in the park.

04:13.174 --> 04:15.675
Lois: Are you and stewie
having a good time?

04:15.677 --> 04:16.943
Uh, uh, yeah.

04:16.945 --> 04:18.444
Okay, well, let me talk to him.

04:18.446 --> 04:20.713
I want to tell him
mommy's on her way home.

04:20.715 --> 04:22.447
She wants to talk to stewie.
What do I do?!

04:22.449 --> 04:24.784
Here, give me the phone.
I do a great stewie.

04:24.786 --> 04:27.086
Hey, lois,
it's me, the baby.

04:27.088 --> 04:29.788
Hi, stewie. I'm on my way home.

04:29.790 --> 04:31.291
Mommy misses you.

04:31.293 --> 04:32.691
All right, cool.

04:32.693 --> 04:34.794
Bring some beef
jerky maybe.

04:34.796 --> 04:38.197
I just bought
you ten minutes.

04:38.199 --> 04:40.165
Stewie?

04:45.070 --> 04:47.472
Oh, there's my boy.

04:49.742 --> 04:51.409
Hey, what happened
to my new friend,

04:51.411 --> 04:53.946
That kid who sort of
looks like me from behind?

04:53.948 --> 04:55.813
Wait. Where's the fat man?

04:55.815 --> 04:58.049
(siren wailing in distance)

04:58.051 --> 04:59.884
Well, I guess this is it.

04:59.886 --> 05:01.419
I'm gonna die here.

05:01.421 --> 05:02.820
I'll never get to grow old

05:02.822 --> 05:04.989
And become an across-the-country
grandparent.

05:04.991 --> 05:06.624
What is this?

05:06.626 --> 05:07.925
Woman:
It's a skype.

05:07.927 --> 05:10.127
A snyke?
No, a skype.

05:10.129 --> 05:11.227
Snype?

05:11.229 --> 05:14.397
No, it's a skype...
From your grandson.

05:14.399 --> 05:15.800
Stephen?

05:15.802 --> 05:18.768
Yes! He's right there
trying to say hi to you.

05:18.770 --> 05:20.271
What movie is this?

05:20.272 --> 05:21.905
It's not a movie.

05:21.907 --> 05:23.606
It's your grandson!

05:23.608 --> 05:25.675
My grandson is in the pictures?

05:25.677 --> 05:27.777
You did this yesterday!

05:27.779 --> 05:29.079
Don't holler at me!

05:29.081 --> 05:30.647
I don't understand anything!

05:30.649 --> 05:32.449
I'm very frightened!

05:32.451 --> 05:35.151
(tires screech)

05:35.753 --> 05:36.986
Wait a minute.

05:36.988 --> 05:40.022
Stewie, what happened
to your head?

05:40.024 --> 05:41.423
Oh, you're not stewie.

05:41.425 --> 05:44.159
I got to get you back
to the park and find...

05:46.663 --> 05:48.397
(gasps)

05:51.935 --> 05:54.103
All right, kid,
your name is stewie, all right?

05:54.105 --> 05:55.504
I'm your new dad.

05:55.506 --> 05:57.873
My name is peter,
and I work at the brewer...

05:57.875 --> 06:01.010
Nasa. I work at nasa.

06:01.644 --> 06:03.378
Uh, hey, lois.

06:03.380 --> 06:06.447
You look fat. You
should go for a run.
Peter!

06:06.449 --> 06:08.717
I'm gonna go give my
baby a kiss good night.

06:08.719 --> 06:12.120
Uh, lois, I had an affair, and
I think we should talk about it!

06:12.122 --> 06:15.590
Peter, jamming yourself into
a grapefruit is not an affair.

06:19.728 --> 06:22.696
See? There's a human baby
in there.

06:22.698 --> 06:24.732
Asleep in stewie's overalls.

06:24.734 --> 06:26.733
Peter, please get
out of my way!

06:26.735 --> 06:27.902
Aah!

06:27.904 --> 06:29.002
Baby:
Aah!
Aah!

06:29.004 --> 06:30.070
(doorbell rings)

06:30.072 --> 06:32.372
Great. We woke up the doorbell.

06:33.241 --> 06:35.075
I think there was
a mix-up at the park.

06:35.077 --> 06:37.244
(gasps)
my little stewie!

06:37.246 --> 06:38.678
Oh, jacob!

06:38.680 --> 06:40.747
Wh-where's your little hat?

06:40.749 --> 06:41.882
He didn't have a hat.

06:41.884 --> 06:43.550
Oh, I am so sorry.

06:43.552 --> 06:44.884
I just got
home myself.

06:44.886 --> 06:46.386
I left my husband in charge,

06:46.388 --> 06:48.888
Which was obviously
a terrible mistake.

06:48.890 --> 06:51.891
Thank you so much.

06:51.893 --> 06:53.993
I took a bath
with the dad.

06:53.995 --> 06:56.395
Mmm. Oh, my baby's
back home.

06:56.397 --> 06:57.763
Mommy missed you.

06:57.765 --> 06:59.098
Congratulations, lois.

06:59.100 --> 07:00.666
You passed the test.

07:00.668 --> 07:01.934
You really do
love stewie.

07:01.936 --> 07:03.569
Now, what do you
say we all sit down

07:03.571 --> 07:06.072
And watch this weird al
yankovic documentary?

07:06.074 --> 07:08.407
<i>It's called
an inconvenient tooth.</i>

07:08.409 --> 07:10.909
(laughing)
what's wrong
with you, peter?!

07:10.911 --> 07:12.178
Lois, I'm sorry.

07:12.180 --> 07:13.912
How the hell
can you possibly

07:13.914 --> 07:15.180
Mistake another baby
for stewie?!

07:15.182 --> 07:16.614
Now, calm down, lois.

07:16.616 --> 07:18.249
You're gonna say
something you don't mean.

07:18.251 --> 07:20.919
Oh, no, I'm not!
You're an idiot!

07:20.921 --> 07:23.121
You don't mean that.

07:23.123 --> 07:25.523
I already got a facebook
friend request from the dad.

07:25.525 --> 07:26.958
Is that weird?

07:26.960 --> 07:29.294
Peter, I have put up
with your nonsense for 20 years,

07:29.296 --> 07:31.029
But today
you crossed a line.

07:31.031 --> 07:33.230
You left a helpless baby
in a public park.

07:33.232 --> 07:36.300
And that's something
only an idiot would do!

07:37.102 --> 07:39.037
<i>I'm not an idiot.</i>

07:39.039 --> 07:41.105
(knocking)

07:41.107 --> 07:44.341
Hey, I think
there was a mix-up at the park.

07:51.082 --> 07:53.383
<i>Man (over tv): We now return
to the karate kid,</i>

07:53.385 --> 07:55.252
With realistic human feelings.

07:55.254 --> 07:57.154
You're all
right, larusso!
(crowd cheering)

07:57.156 --> 07:59.889
(bleep) you just tried
to cripple me!

07:59.891 --> 08:01.458
(sighs)

08:01.460 --> 08:03.993
I hate to sound like every
woman ever, but I'm depressed.

08:03.995 --> 08:05.561
Don't engage.
Don't engage.

08:05.563 --> 08:06.829
Why?
Damn it!

08:06.831 --> 08:08.564
Lois called
me an idiot.
So?

08:08.566 --> 08:11.234
So, I don't tell her all the
bad things about herself.

08:11.236 --> 08:13.069
Like how the mole on her back

08:13.071 --> 08:15.170
Is changing shape and
size really quickly.

08:15.172 --> 08:17.073
Being dumb isn't
the worst thing, peter.

08:17.075 --> 08:18.807
At least you're not
two foreign guys

08:18.809 --> 08:21.077
Talking too loud
in the next booth.

08:21.079 --> 08:23.078
Much sorry, friend!

08:23.080 --> 08:25.514
Man, there are
no womens here.

08:25.516 --> 08:28.817
We've got to make like '70s
rock man garrett and leave.

08:28.819 --> 08:30.118
You said it, belgard.

08:30.120 --> 08:32.287
Looks like you and me
will have to make hands

08:32.289 --> 08:33.588
On each other tonight.

08:33.590 --> 08:34.956
Aah, gross!

08:34.958 --> 08:37.192
(laughs) I was just
playing joke at you!

08:37.194 --> 08:39.261
Ah, good one! You
should be comedy writer.

08:39.263 --> 08:40.628
Too late, friend.

08:40.630 --> 08:42.831
I already have
comedy development at cbs.

08:42.833 --> 08:44.098
Oh, nice!

08:44.100 --> 08:45.867
Cbs knows real situations

08:45.869 --> 08:47.668
I want to see
for 100 episodes!

08:47.670 --> 08:50.704
Thanks. My hysterical
multi-camera show is called

08:50.706 --> 08:53.275
<i>Wizard robot and his
less successful friend.</i>

08:53.277 --> 08:56.043
Oh, man, you know
what america wants.

08:56.045 --> 08:58.045
All right, fine, so
I'm a dumb, hot guy.

08:58.047 --> 08:59.713
All right? There's
worse things to be.

08:59.715 --> 09:01.615
Okay, we're only gonna
tackle one thing today.

09:01.617 --> 09:04.017
Peter, maybe you need to
broaden your horizons, you know?

09:04.019 --> 09:05.352
Read a book, travel.

09:05.354 --> 09:06.986
Oh, yeah, I love traveling.

09:06.988 --> 09:08.222
You see new things,

09:08.224 --> 09:09.889
Inconvenience thousands
of people.

09:09.891 --> 09:11.558
You know what?
You guys are right.

09:11.560 --> 09:14.627
It's time to travel, to learn,
to experience new things.

09:14.629 --> 09:16.896
I've been letting opportunities
pass me by

09:16.898 --> 09:18.631
Ever since I was a kid.

09:19.833 --> 09:23.169
Hey, kid, get in my van, and
I'll give you some candy.

09:23.171 --> 09:26.471
No, my mom says I shouldn't.

09:30.476 --> 09:33.312
(crying)

09:33.314 --> 09:37.382
Hey, kid, get in my van, and
I'll give you some candy.

09:37.384 --> 09:39.451
Okay!

09:47.227 --> 09:50.262
Stella, I need you to go
to chicago on Thursday.

09:50.264 --> 09:54.166
I can't. This week
is the deaf games.

09:54.168 --> 09:56.500
(bell clanging)

09:58.104 --> 10:00.104
(bell continues clanging)

10:00.106 --> 10:02.373
Oh, my god, this has been
a 12-minute round.

10:02.375 --> 10:05.109
Why does every fight
have to go to the death?

10:05.111 --> 10:06.444
Angela, if you got
business traveling

10:06.446 --> 10:08.679
That needs to be done,
I'm your guy.

10:08.681 --> 10:10.281
Griffin, I'm not
gonna look over there

10:10.283 --> 10:12.550
Until you first assure
me you've got pants on.

10:12.552 --> 10:15.218
It's not a rule unless
there's a sign on the wall.

10:15.220 --> 10:17.221
I won that court case.
Fine.

10:17.223 --> 10:19.055
So you'd be willing
to take that trip

10:19.057 --> 10:20.391
To chicago for
the company?

10:20.393 --> 10:22.058
Yeah, you know,
I was just saying

10:22.060 --> 10:23.294
I need to broaden my horizons.

10:23.296 --> 10:24.894
You see, my wife thinks
I'm an idiot.

10:24.896 --> 10:27.231
She's always making me feel
small and insignificant.

10:27.233 --> 10:29.266
Like john goodman's
heartbeat.

10:29.268 --> 10:31.701
(heart thumps)

10:31.703 --> 10:35.405
Honey? My inside left boob
stomach did that thing again.

10:35.407 --> 10:37.106
You mean
your heart?

10:37.108 --> 10:39.409
Um, I don't know
about any of that,

10:39.411 --> 10:41.944
But I think
I should eat something.

10:45.315 --> 10:47.249
Well, gentlemen,
thank you for coming.

10:47.251 --> 10:49.418
Mr. Griffin, I believe you
have something for me.

10:49.420 --> 10:51.387
Yes, I do, mr. Franks.
Terrific.

10:51.389 --> 10:53.389
We were completely
out of these tubes.

10:53.391 --> 10:55.324
Well, thank you all
for coming. Good day.

10:55.326 --> 10:57.326
Nicely done,
mr. Franks.
Thanks, chief.

10:57.328 --> 10:59.395
Wait, so that's it?
Hey, you nailed it!

10:59.397 --> 11:00.963
But I'm here till
tomorrow night.

11:00.965 --> 11:02.398
What am I
supposed to do?

11:02.400 --> 11:04.065
Get out there
and explore chicago, peter.

11:04.067 --> 11:06.234
It's one of the great cities
of the world.

11:06.236 --> 11:09.071
There's museums,
a symphony, a lyric opera.

11:09.073 --> 11:10.338
Whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa.

11:10.340 --> 11:12.241
Did you say "chicken
fashion show"?

11:12.243 --> 11:13.741
No.
Oh.

11:13.743 --> 11:15.843
But that-that other stuff,
they all sound like

11:15.845 --> 11:19.647
The kind of things I could
do to expand my horizons.

11:20.949 --> 11:22.116
Wow.

11:22.118 --> 11:24.819
Chicago:
"the san francisco treat."

11:24.821 --> 11:27.121
I haven't felt this sense
of limitless adventure

11:27.123 --> 11:29.122
Since I went cave jumping.

11:29.124 --> 11:30.757
Here we go!

11:30.759 --> 11:34.996
(echoing): I told no one
what I was doing today!

11:38.666 --> 11:42.936
Man, I'm, like, the fifth most
attractive woman in chicago.

11:49.376 --> 11:51.178
Hi. Welcome
to the museum.

11:51.180 --> 11:52.978
Thanks.
Just to be clear,

11:52.980 --> 11:54.314
I should touch
everything, right?

11:54.316 --> 11:55.881
No, please don't
touch anything.

11:55.883 --> 11:58.351
Sorry, it's my first time
at an adult museum.

11:58.353 --> 11:59.985
I'm used to petting
the starfishes.

11:59.987 --> 12:02.154
Well, maybe you'd find
our audio tour helpful.

12:02.156 --> 12:03.723
You have your choice
of narrators:

12:03.725 --> 12:05.157
Our senior curator

12:05.159 --> 12:07.559
Or chicago's own
dennis farina.

12:07.561 --> 12:09.729
Hmm.

12:09.731 --> 12:12.131
Farina: Hey there, chief.
Dennis farina here.

12:12.133 --> 12:13.799
And welcome to our museum.

12:13.801 --> 12:17.369
Just so you know, I'll be
eating through most of this.

12:17.371 --> 12:19.471
Yeah. This one.

12:20.307 --> 12:22.207
Farina:
(chewing) ah, man,

12:22.209 --> 12:24.142
That's good sausage.
(burps)

12:24.144 --> 12:25.377
Oops. Excuse me.

12:25.379 --> 12:27.545
<i>Anyways, this is
at the moulin rouge</i>

12:27.547 --> 12:29.047
By toulouse-lautrec.

12:29.049 --> 12:30.748
Uh, it's from the 1890s.

12:30.750 --> 12:34.953
Now, he was a midge,
but he painted like a normal.

12:36.721 --> 12:40.257
Now, here is a naked chick
made completely out of marble.

12:40.259 --> 12:42.394
I got to wonder--
I'm sure you do, too--

12:42.396 --> 12:45.362
How this thing didn't crack
when they were carving out

12:45.364 --> 12:47.431
Her downstairs business.

12:47.433 --> 12:50.401
(loudly): He did a great job
with the vagina.

12:50.403 --> 12:53.202
Here's a picture
by this guy salvador dalн.

12:53.204 --> 12:56.706
This guy, I'm telling you,
was a freakin' whack-a-doodle.

12:56.708 --> 13:00.209
Wow, who knew you could learn
so much at a museum?

13:00.211 --> 13:01.845
And this is only chicago.

13:01.847 --> 13:04.380
From now on, I'm gonna volunteer
for every business trip,

